  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize leading ranks of which you hold multiple cards. If you hold three of a kind, you can almost guarantee being the one to play the 'best of all the three,' but you'll need the 4th player to enable you or wait for someone else to lead the 4th.\n\nLeading Pairs: Leading from a pair is safe, as it allows you to maintain some control over when that rank is exhausted.\n\nStop Tracking: Keep track of which ranks have already had their 4th card ('the Earl') played. Once a 4th card is played, that rank is 'dead'. Use this knowledge to determine which other ranks are likely to be playable.",
    Player: "Prioritize leading ranks of which you hold multiple cards. If you hold three of a kind, you can almost guarantee being the one to play the 'best of all the three,' but you'll need the 4th player to enable you or wait for someone else to lead the 4th.\n\nLeading Pairs: Leading from a pair is safe, as it allows you to maintain some control over when that rank is exhausted.\n\nStop Tracking: Keep track of which ranks have already had their 4th card ('the Earl') played. Once a 4th card is played, that rank is 'dead'. Use this knowledge to determine which other ranks are likely to be playable.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
